# Scripts that run on Linux must keep LF endings in the WORKING COPY, not just in the blob.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine, so without this a checkout rewrites these files to CRLF and a
# tarball built from the working tree ships them to Sherlock with \r line endings. bash then fails on
# the first line it reads -- `$'\r': command not found`, or a silently mangled `set -euo pipefail` --
# which is a confusing failure to debug from a SLURM log. The blobs are already LF; this pins the
# checkout to match.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
